        <p>The practical impact on shipping remains severe. With active mine-laying confirmed and now military strikes in the immediate vicinity, the already minimal commercial traffic through Hormuz is likely to drop to near-zero for the coming days. Insurance premiums for any vessel attempting transit have effectively become prohibitive, with war risk rates now exceeding 5% of hull value. The longer-term consequences will depend critically on Iran's response: a measured diplomatic protest would signal de-escalation is possible, while retaliatory military action could trigger a far wider regional conflict.</p>
